        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Salicornia fruticosa, synonym Sarcocornia fruticosa, known commonly as the shrubby marsh samphire, is a species of glasswort in the family Amaranthaceae (pigweeds). It is native to southern Europe, north Africa, Western Asia and Yemen. It is a halophyte, a plant that can grow in saline conditions."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "It is the main saltwort species used in making special pot ash made during Mesopotamian times to the early Islamic era – قَلَيّ qali – which is the basis for the word \"alkali\"."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
